  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 1; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works con...\n- {\"content\":\"Emily can peel \\\\(7\\\\) shrimp per minute for \\\\(10\\\\) minutes:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n7 \\\\times 10 = 70\\n\\\\]\\n\\nSince \\\\(70 \\\\le 100\\\\), she has enough shrimp available. Therefore,\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{70}\\n\\\\]\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Emily can peel 6 shrimp per minute.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel \\(6\\) shrimp per minute for \\(10\\) minutes:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nSince \\(60 \\le 100\\), she has enough shrimp available. Therefore,\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{60}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now let me ask about just one part of that. How many shrimp can Emily peel in ten minutes? Additionally, Emily discards 5 shrimp after peeling them because they are damaged.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nShe discards \\(5\\) damaged shrimp afterward, leaving:\n\n\\[\n60 - 5 = 55\n\\]\n\nSo, Emily can peel \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp, of which \\(\\boxed{55}\\) remain usable.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 12 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel \\(60\\) shrimp in ten minutes and, after discarding \\(5\\), has \\(55\\) usable shrimp.\n\nHer sautéing rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{30}{12}=2.5\\text{ shrimp per minute}\n\\]\n\nThus, in ten minutes she can sauté:\n\n\\[\n2.5 \\times 10=25\n\\]\n\nSo she can sauté \\(\\boxed{25}\\) shrimp in ten minutes, assuming she has enough peeled shrimp ready.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can sauté \\(30\\) shrimp in \\(10\\) minutes. Since \\(55\\) usable shrimp are available after peeling and discarding the damaged ones, she has enough.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Emily peels and sautés each shrimp sequentially:\n\n- Peeling one shrimp takes \\(\\frac{60}{6}=10\\) seconds.\n- Sautéing one shrimp takes \\(\\frac{600}{30}=20\\) seconds.\n- Total time per shrimp is \\(10+20=30\\) seconds.\n\nIn \\(10\\) minutes (\\(600\\) seconds), she can process:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{600}{30}=20\\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nAfter discarding \\(5\\) damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n20-5=15\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Emily can sauté \\(\\boxed{15}\\) usable shrimp.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily’s rates are:\n\n- Peeling: \\(6\\) shrimp/minute, so \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) minute per shrimp.\n- Sautéing: \\(30\\) shrimp in \\(10\\) minutes \\(=3\\) shrimp/minute, so \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) minute per shrimp.\n\nBecause she works sequentially, each shrimp takes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ minute}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(5\\) shrimp are discarded, she must peel \\(90+5=95\\) shrimp to end up cooking \\(90\\).\n\n\\[\n95\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=47.5\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, it will take Emily\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{47.5\\text{ minutes}}\n\\]\n\nto peel and cook \\(90\\) usable shrimp.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
